-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- service out of Singapore`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 3(1): the Rule applies to limitation actions and to actions commenced by originating claim containing a claim for damage, loss of life or
-- personal injury arising out of (a) a collision between ships, (b) a manoeuvre, or (c) non-compliance with the collision regulations.
-- src:4594 | 3. —(1) This Rule applies to limitation actions, and to actions commenced by originating claim containing a claim for damage, loss of life or personal injury arising out of — ( a )
-- src:4595 | a collision between ships;
-- src:4596 | ( b )
-- src:4597 | the carrying out of or omission to carry out a manoeuvre in the case of one or more of 2 or more ships; or
-- src:4598 | ( c )
-- src:4599 | non‑compliance on the part of one or more of 2 or more ships with the collision regulations.
@ref O 33 r 3(1) (src:4594-4599)
GIVEN `the action is a limitation action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is commenced by originating claim containing a claim for damage, loss of life or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim arises out of a collision between ships` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim arises out of the carrying out of or omission to carry out a manoeuvre in the case of one or more of 2 or more ships` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim arises out of non-compliance on the part of one or more of 2 or more ships with the collision regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 3(1) this Rule applies to the action` MEANS
    IF `the action is a limitation action` OR (`the action is commenced by originating claim containing a claim for damage, loss of life or personal injury` AND (`the claim arises out of a collision between ships` OR `the claim arises out of the carrying out of or omission to carry out a manoeuvre in the case of one or more of 2 or more ships` OR `the claim arises out of non-compliance on the part of one or more of 2 or more ships with the collision regulations`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Rule applies to" the actions named, and does not say it applies only to them

-- r 3(2): service out of Singapore is permissible with the permission of the Court if any of four grounds holds.
-- src:4600 | (2) Subject to the provisions of this Rule, service out of Singapore of an originating claim for a limitation action, or an originating claim containing a claim mentioned in paragraph (1) is permissible with the permission of the Court if — ( a )
-- src:4601 | the defendant has the defendant’s habitual residence or a place of business within Singapore;
-- src:4602 | ( b )
-- src:4603 | the cause of action arose within inland waters of Singapore or within the limits of the port of Singapore;
-- src:4604 | ( c )
-- src:4605 | an action arising out of the same incident or series of incidents is proceeding in the General Division or has been heard and determined in the General Division; or
-- src:4606 | ( d )
-- src:4607 | the defendant has submitted or agreed to submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division.
@ref O 33 r 3(2) (src:4600-4607)
GIVEN `the originating claim is for a limitation action or contains a claim mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has the defendant's habitual residence or a place of business within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action arose within inland waters of Singapore or within the limits of the port of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an action arising out of the same incident or series of incidents is proceeding in the General Division or has been heard and determined in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has submitted or agreed to submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 3(2) service out of Singapore is permissible` MEANS
    IF `the originating claim is for a limitation action or contains a claim mentioned in paragraph (1)` AND (`the defendant has the defendant's habitual residence or a place of business within Singapore` OR `the cause of action arose within inland waters of Singapore or within the limits of the port of Singapore` OR `an action arising out of the same incident or series of incidents is proceeding in the General Division or has been heard and determined in the General Division` OR `the defendant has submitted or agreed to submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division`)
    THEN IF `the Court has given permission`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is permissible with the permission of the Court": no permission yet
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is permissible with the permission of the Court if" one of the four grounds holds

-- src:4608 | (3) This Rule does not apply to an action in rem .
@ref O 33 r 3(3) (src:4608)
GIVEN `the action is an action in rem` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 3(3) this Rule applies to the action` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action in rem`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule does not apply to an action in rem"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of these facts
-- src:4609 | (4) Order 8 (except Rule 4) applies to service out of Singapore under this Rule.
@ref O 33 r 3(4) (src:4609)
GIVEN `the service is service out of Singapore under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 3(4) Order 8 other than Rule 4 applies to the service out of Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the service is service out of Singapore under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Order 8 (except Rule 4) applies to service out of Singapore under this Rule"
-- src:4610 | (5) In this Rule, “collision regulations”, “inland waters of Singapore” and “port of Singapore” have the meanings given by the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act.
@ref O 33 r 3(5) (src:4610)
GIVEN `the term is “collision regulations”, “inland waters of Singapore” or “port of Singapore”` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meaning is the one given by the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 3(5) a term has the meaning given by the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act` MEANS
    IF `the term is “collision regulations”, “inland waters of Singapore” or “port of Singapore”` AND `the meaning is the one given by the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Rule, “collision regulations”, “inland waters of Singapore” and “port of Singapore” have the meanings given by the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- warrant of arrest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4612 | 4. —(1) In an action in rem the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may, after the issue of the originating claim in the action and subject to the provisions of this Rule, apply for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought. (2) Before a warrant to arrest any property is issued, a party applying for it must — ( a )
@ref O 33 r 4(1) (src:4612)
GIVEN `the action is an action in rem` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating claim in the action has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(1) the claimant or defendant may apply for a warrant of arrest` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action in rem` AND `the originating claim in the action has been issued`
    THEN IF `the application is for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an action in rem the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may, after the issue of the originating claim in the action and subject to the provisions of this Rule, apply for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In an action in rem the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may, after the issue of the originating claim in the action and subject to the provisions of this Rule, apply for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought"
-- src:4612 | 4. —(1) In an action in rem the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) may, after the issue of the originating claim in the action and subject to the provisions of this Rule, apply for a warrant in Form 51 for the arrest of the property against which the action or any counterclaim in the action is brought. (2) Before a warrant to arrest any property is issued, a party applying for it must — ( a )
-- src:4613 | file a warrant in Form 51; and
-- src:4614 | ( b )
-- src:4615 | procure a search to be made in the record of caveats for the purpose of ascertaining whether there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to that property.
@ref O 33 r 4(2) (src:4612-4615)
GIVEN `a warrant to arrest any property is to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party applying files a warrant in Form 51` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party applying procures a search to be made in the record of caveats for the purpose of ascertaining whether there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to that property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(2) the party applying for a warrant files it and procures a search of the record of caveats` MEANS
    IF `a warrant to arrest any property is to be issued`
    THEN IF `the party applying files a warrant in Form 51` AND `the party applying procures a search to be made in the record of caveats for the purpose of ascertaining whether there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to that property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Before a warrant to arrest any property is issued, a party applying for it must — file a warrant in Form 51; and procure a search to be made in the record of caveats for the purpose of ascertaining whether there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to that property" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 4(2) the party applying for a warrant files it and procures a search of the record of caveats (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 4(2) (src:4612-4615)
GIVEN `a warrant to arrest any property is to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(2) the party applying for a warrant files it and procures a search of the record of caveats (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `a warrant to arrest any property is to be issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before a warrant to arrest any property is issued, a party applying for it must — file a warrant in Form 51; and procure a search to be made in the record of caveats for the purpose of ascertaining whether there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to that property"

-- r 4(3): "must not be issued until" the affidavit is filed (the bar is its own yes/no function: ruling 2026-11-05 (d)); "however, the Court may allow".
-- src:4616 | (3) A warrant of arrest must not be issued until the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party’s agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7); however, the Court may, if the Court thinks fit, allow the warrant to issue even though the affidavit does not contain all those particulars.
@ref O 33 r 4(3) (src:4616)
GIVEN `the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party's agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(3) the warrant of arrest cannot yet be issued for want of the affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party's agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be issued until the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit": the affidavit is filed
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4616 | (3) A warrant of arrest must not be issued until the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party’s agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7); however, the Court may, if the Court thinks fit, allow the warrant to issue even though the affidavit does not contain all those particulars.
@ref O 33 r 4(3) however (src:4616)
GIVEN `the affidavit has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit does not contain all the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit and allows the warrant to issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(3) the Court may allow the warrant to issue although the affidavit lacks particulars` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit has been filed` AND `the affidavit does not contain all the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)`
    THEN IF `the Court thinks fit and allows the warrant to issue`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, if the Court thinks fit, allow the warrant to issue even though the affidavit does not contain all those particulars"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may, if the Court thinks fit, allow the warrant to issue even though the affidavit does not contain all those particulars"

-- r 4(3), the permission question: with the affidavit filed the bar is lifted, and the paragraph does not say that the warrant must then be issued.
@ref O 33 r 4(3) permission question (src:4616)
GIVEN `the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party's agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has allowed the warrant to issue although the affidavit does not contain all those particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(3) a warrant of arrest may be issued` MEANS
    IF `the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit made by that party or that party's agent containing the particulars required by paragraphs (6) and (7)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the affidavit is filed, so the "until" bar has ended; the sentence does not say that the warrant is then issued (open convention question QA)
    ELSE IF `the Court has allowed the warrant to issue although the affidavit does not contain all those particulars`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- "the Court may, if the Court thinks fit, allow the warrant to issue even though the affidavit does not contain all those particulars": the Court's allowance is the permission the sentence gives (open convention question QA)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A warrant of arrest must not be issued until the party applying for the warrant has filed an affidavit"

-- r 4(4): the same shape, for a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore, in an action for possession or wages.
-- src:4617 | (4) Except with the permission of the Court, a warrant of arrest must not be issued in an action in rem against a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore, being an action for possession of the ship or for wages, until notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul.
@ref O 33 r 4(4) (src:4617)
GIVEN `the action is an action in rem against a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is an action for possession of the ship or for wages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(4) the warrant of arrest cannot yet be issued for want of notice to the consul` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action in rem against a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore` AND `the action is an action for possession of the ship or for wages`
    THEN IF `notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul": the notice is sent
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (4) speaks only of a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate, in an action for possession or wages

@ref O 33 r 4(4) permission question (src:4617)
GIVEN `the action is an action in rem against a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is an action for possession of the ship or for wages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(4) a warrant of arrest may be issued against the foreign ship` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action in rem against a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate in Singapore` AND `the action is an action for possession of the ship or for wages`
    THEN IF `notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the notice has been sent to the consul, so the "until" bar has ended; the sentence does not say that the warrant is then issued (open convention question QA)
         ELSE IF `the Court has given permission`
              THEN JUST TRUE -- "Except with the permission of the Court": the permission is the exception the sentence gives, so the warrant may be issued (open convention question QA)
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the permission of the Court, a warrant of arrest must not be issued ... until notice that the action has been begun has been sent to the consul"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (4) speaks only of a foreign ship belonging to a port of a state having a consulate, in an action for possession or wages

-- src:4618 | (5) Issue of a warrant of arrest takes place upon its being sealed by an officer of the Registry.
