      `it states the nature of the claim or counterclaim in respect of which the warrant is required and that it has not been satisfied and, if it arises in connection with a ship, the name of that ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the nature of the property to be arrested and, if the property is a ship, the name of the ship and the port of her registry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(6) the affidavit states what paragraph (6) requires` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is one required by paragraph (3)`
    THEN IF `it states the name, address and occupation of the applicant for the warrant` AND `it states the nature of the claim or counterclaim in respect of which the warrant is required and that it has not been satisfied and, if it arises in connection with a ship, the name of that ship` AND `it states the nature of the property to be arrested and, if the property is a ship, the name of the ship and the port of her registry`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Every affidavit required by paragraph (3) must state — the name, address and occupation of the applicant for the warrant; the nature of the claim or counterclaim in respect of which the warrant is required and that it has not been satisfied and, if it arises in connection with a ship, the name of that ship; and the nature of the property to be arrested and, if the property is a ship, the name of the ship and the port of her registry" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 4(6) the affidavit states what paragraph (6) requires (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 4(6) (src:4619-4624)
GIVEN `the affidavit is one required by paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(6) the affidavit states what paragraph (6) requires (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is one required by paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every affidavit required by paragraph (3) must state — the name, address and occupation of the applicant for the warrant; the nature of the claim or counterclaim in respect of which the warrant is required and that it has not been satisfied and, if it arises in connection with a ship, the name of that ship; and the nature of the property to be arrested and, if the property is a ship, the name of the ship and the port of her registry"

-- r 4(7): an affidavit in an action in rem against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act must state (a) to (d); (d) bites only in a possession or wages claim.
-- src:4625 | (7) Every affidavit in an action in rem brought against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act, must state — ( a )
-- src:4626 | the name of the person who would be liable on the claim in an action in personam (the relevant person);
-- src:4627 | ( b )
-- src:4628 | that the relevant person was when the cause of action arose the owner or charterer of, or in possession or in control of, the ship in connection with which the claim arose;
-- src:4629 | ( c )
-- src:4630 | that at the time of the issue of the originating claim, the relevant person was either the beneficial owner of all the shares in the ship in respect of which the warrant is required or the charterer of that ship under a charter by demise; and
-- src:4631 | ( d )
-- src:4632 | in the case of a claim for possession of a ship or for wages, the nationality of the ship in respect of which the warrant is required, and that the notice (if any) required by paragraph (4) has been sent.
@ref O 33 r 4(7) (src:4625-4632)
GIVEN `the affidavit is in an action in rem brought against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the name of the person who would be liable on the claim in an action in personam (the relevant person)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the relevant person was when the cause of action arose the owner or charterer of, or in possession or in control of, the ship in connection with which the claim arose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that at the time of the issue of the originating claim the relevant person was either the beneficial owner of all the shares in the ship in respect of which the warrant is required or the charterer of that ship under a charter by demise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is a claim for possession of a ship or for wages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the nationality of the ship in respect of which the warrant is required and that the notice (if any) required by paragraph (4) has been sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(7) the affidavit states what paragraph (7) requires` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is in an action in rem brought against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act`
    THEN IF `it states the name of the person who would be liable on the claim in an action in personam (the relevant person)` AND `it states that the relevant person was when the cause of action arose the owner or charterer of, or in possession or in control of, the ship in connection with which the claim arose` AND `it states that at the time of the issue of the originating claim the relevant person was either the beneficial owner of all the shares in the ship in respect of which the warrant is required or the charterer of that ship under a charter by demise` AND ((NOT `the claim is a claim for possession of a ship or for wages`) OR `it states the nationality of the ship in respect of which the warrant is required and that the notice (if any) required by paragraph (4) has been sent`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): a bare "must state": the statement is not yet made (open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 4(7) the affidavit states what paragraph (7) requires (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)

@ref O 33 r 4(7) the duty arises (src:4625)
GIVEN `the affidavit is in an action in rem brought against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 4(7) the affidavit states what paragraph (7) requires (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is in an action in rem brought against a ship by virtue of section 4(4) of the High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 5 and 6 -- caveat against arrest; remedy where protected property is arrested`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4634 | 5. —(1) A person who desires to prevent the arrest of any property must file in the Registry a caveat, in Form 52, signed by the person’s solicitor undertaking — ( a )
-- src:4635 | to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property described in the caveat; and
-- src:4636 | ( b )
-- src:4637 | within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun, to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court,
-- src:4638 | and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats.
@ref O 33 r 5(1) (src:4634-4638)
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 52` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats` MEANS
    IF `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property`
    THEN IF `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 52` AND `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property` AND `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court` AND `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "A person who desires to prevent the arrest of any property must file in the Registry a caveat, in Form 52, signed by the person’s solicitor undertaking — to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property described in the caveat; and within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun, to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court, and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 5(1) (src:4634-4638)
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who desires to prevent the arrest of any property must file in the Registry a caveat, in Form 52, signed by the person’s solicitor undertaking — to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property described in the caveat; and within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun, to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court, and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats"
-- src:4636 | ( b )
-- src:4637 | within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun, to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court,
-- src:4638 | and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats.
@ref O 33 r 5(1)(b) 3 days (src:4636-4638)
`o 33 r 5(1)(b) the period for giving bail or paying into Court` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 33 r 5(1)(b) 3 days (src:4636-4638)
