-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- service of originating claim in an action in rem`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4643 | 7. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), an originating claim by which an action in rem is begun must be served on the property against which the action is brought except — ( a )
-- src:4644 | where the property is freight, in which case it must be served on the cargo in respect of which the freight is payable or on the ship in which that cargo was carried; or
-- src:4645 | ( b )
-- src:4646 | where the property has been sold by the Sheriff, in which case the originating claim may not be served on that property but a sealed copy of it must be filed in the Registry and served on the Sheriff, and the originating claim is deemed to have been served on the day on which the copy was filed.
@ref O 33 r 7(1) (src:4643-4646)
GIVEN `an originating claim begins an action in rem` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is neither freight nor property sold by the Sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating claim is not deemed to have been duly served on the defendant by virtue of paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating claim is served on the property against which the action is brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 7(1) the originating claim is served on the property against which the action is brought` MEANS
    IF `an originating claim begins an action in rem`
    THEN IF `the property is neither freight nor property sold by the Sheriff` AND `the originating claim is not deemed to have been duly served on the defendant by virtue of paragraph (3)`
         THEN IF `the originating claim is served on the property against which the action is brought`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Subject to paragraph (2), an originating claim by which an action in rem is begun must be served on the property against which the action is brought except — where the property is freight ... or where the property has been sold by the Sheriff" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the exception applies, so the requirement does not apply: "Subject to paragraph (2), an originating claim by which an action in rem is begun must be served on the property against which the action is brought except — where the property is freight ... or where the property has been sold by the Sheriff"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 7(1) the originating claim is served on the property against which the action is brought (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 7(1) (src:4643-4646)
GIVEN `an originating claim begins an action in rem` IS A BOOLEAN
