-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 10 and 11 -- service on ships, etc.: how effected, and during the relevant period`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4681 | 10. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and Rule 11, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo must be effected — ( a )
-- src:4682 | by affixing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure; and
-- src:4683 | ( b )
-- src:4684 | on removing the warrant or originating claim, by leaving a copy of it affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship.
@ref O 33 r 10(1) (src:4681-4684)
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant or originating claim is affixed for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on removing it, a copy is left affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy` MEANS
    IF `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo`
    THEN IF `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies`
         THEN IF `the warrant or originating claim is affixed for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure` AND `on removing it, a copy is left affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Subject to paragraph (2) and Rule 11, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo must be effected — by affixing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure; and on removing the warrant or originating claim, by leaving a copy of it affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the exception applies, so the requirement does not apply: "Subject to paragraph (2) and Rule 11, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo must be effected — by affixing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure; and on removing the warrant or originating claim, by leaving a copy of it affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 10(1) (src:4681-4684)
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` AND `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2) and Rule 11, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo must be effected — by affixing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure; and on removing the warrant or originating claim, by leaving a copy of it affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship"

-- src:4685 | (2) Service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both must, if the cargo has been landed or transhipped, be effected — ( a )
