-- r 11(1): service by (a) leaving a copy with the agent AND (b) transmitting by fax or email.  The "and" is read as both (fork F-33-1).
-- src:4690 | 11. —(1) Despite Rules 9(6) and 10(1), but subject to Rule 10(2), during the relevant period, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo may be effected — ( a )
-- src:4691 | by leaving a copy of the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) with the agent of the ship or, in any case where the agent of the ship is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent of the ship; and
-- src:4692 | ( b )
-- src:4693 | by transmitting the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) in either of the following ways: (i)
-- src:4694 | by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent of the ship as the fax number of that agent;
-- src:4695 | (ii)
-- src:4696 | by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent of the ship as the electronic mail address of that agent.
@ref O 33 r 11(1) (src:4690-4696)
GIVEN `it is the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 10(2) does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is left with the agent of the ship or, where the agent is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant or originating claim is transmitted by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent or by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 11(1) service may be effected on the agent of the ship during the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `it is the relevant period` AND `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` AND `Rule 10(2) does not apply`
    THEN IF `a copy is left with the agent of the ship or, where the agent is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent` AND `the warrant or originating claim is transmitted by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent or by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite Rules 9(6) and 10(1), but subject to Rule 10(2), during the relevant period, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo may be effected — by leaving a copy of the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) with the agent of the ship or, in any case where the agent of the ship is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent of the ship; and by transmitting the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) in either of the following ways"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite Rules 9(6) and 10(1), but subject to Rule 10(2), during the relevant period, service of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo may be effected — by leaving a copy of the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) with the agent of the ship or, in any case where the agent of the ship is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent of the ship; and by transmitting the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) in either of the following ways"
-- src:4697 | (2) Where the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1) — ( a )
-- src:4698 | the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) is deemed to be served on the property against which it is issued; and
@ref O 33 r 11(2)(a) (src:4697-4698)
GIVEN `the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 11(2)(a) the warrant or originating claim is deemed served on the property` MEANS
    IF `the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) is deemed to be served on the property against which it is issued"

-- r 11(2)(b): the time of service is the later of the time the copy is left and the time the whole document is received by fax or email.
-- src:4699 | ( b )
-- src:4700 | the time of service of the warrant of arrest or originating claim is the later of — (i)
-- src:4701 | the time that the warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) is left in accordance with paragraph (1)( a ); and
-- src:4702 | (ii)
-- src:4703 | the time that the entire warrant of arrest or originating claim (as the case may be) is received by fax or electronic mail transmitted in accordance with paragraph (1)( b )(i) or (ii) (whichever is applicable).
@ref O 33 r 11(2)(b) (src:4699-4703)
-- left: the time the warrant of arrest or originating claim is left in accordance with paragraph (1)(a).
-- received: the time the entire warrant of arrest or originating claim is received by fax or electronic mail in accordance with paragraph (1)(b)(i) or (ii).
GIVEN left IS A Moment
      received IS A Moment
GIVETH A Moment
`o 33 r 11(2)(b) the time of service` MEANS
    IF (left's `day of the moment`) LESS THAN (received's `day of the moment`)
    THEN received
    ELSE IF (left's `day of the moment`) GREATER THAN (received's `day of the moment`)
         THEN left
         ELSE IF (left's `minutes after midnight`) AT MOST (received's `minutes after midnight`)
              THEN received
              ELSE left

