-- ANCHOR for the Fourth Schedule (fees for O 33 r 13): a release is issued under this Rule where an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry.
-- src:4746 | 13. —(1) Except where property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest is sold under an order of the Court, property which has been so arrested must only be released under the authority of an instrument of release (called in this Rule a release), in Form 54, issued out of the Registry. (2) A release must not be issued with respect to property as to which a caveat against release is in force, unless, either — ( a )
@ref O 33 r 13 anchor (src:4746)
GIVEN `an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry for property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 13 an instrument of release is issued under this Rule` MEANS
    IF `an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry for property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) says how property is released and does not say that an instrument otherwise issued is not a release under the Rule

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 14 to 17 -- caveat against release and payment; duration of caveats; bail; interveners`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4761 | 14. —(1) A person who desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property must file in the Registry a caveat in Form 55, and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats. (2) Where the release of any property under arrest is delayed by the entry of a caveat under this Rule, any person having an interest in that property may apply to the Court by summons for an order requiring the person who procured the entry of the caveat to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant by reason of the delay, and the Court, unless the Court is satisfied that the person procuring the entry of the caveat had a good and sufficient reason for doing so, may make an order accordingly.
@ref O 33 r 14(1) (src:4761)
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property` IS A BOOLEAN
