-- src:4763 | 15. —(1) Every caveat entered in the record of caveats is valid for 6 months beginning with the date of its entry, but the person at whose instance a caveat was entered may withdraw it by filing a withdrawal of caveat in Form 56. (2) The period of validity of a caveat may not be extended but this provision is not to be taken as preventing the entry of successive caveats.
@ref O 33 r 15(1) (src:4763)
`o 33 r 15(1) the period of validity of the caveat` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 6
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 33 r 15(1) (src:4763)
GIVEN `o 3 r 3 the last day of the validity` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 15(1) the caveat is valid on the date` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day of the validity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (period in its own words): "valid for 6 months beginning with the date of its entry"
