    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The party on whose behalf bail is given must serve on the opposite party a notice of bail containing the names and addresses of the persons who have given bail on that party’s behalf and of the commissioner for oaths or Registrar before whom the bail bond was entered into; and after the expiration of 24 hours after the service of the notice (or sooner with the consent of the opposite party), that party may file the bond and must at the same time file the affidavits (if any) made under paragraph (2), and an affidavit proving due service of the notice of bail to which a copy of that notice must be exhibited"

-- r 16(4): the bond may be filed after the expiration of 24 hours after service of the notice, or sooner with the opposite party's consent.
@ref O 33 r 16(4) 24 hours (src:4767)
-- served: the moment the notice of bail was served.  filed: the moment of filing the bond.
GIVEN served IS A Moment
      filed IS A Moment
      `the opposite party has consented to filing sooner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 16(4) the bond may be filed at the moment` MEANS
    IF `the opposite party has consented to filing sooner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (served's `day of the moment`) PLUS 1 LESS THAN (filed's `day of the moment`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (served's `day of the moment`) PLUS 1 EQUALS (filed's `day of the moment`)
              THEN IF (filed's `minutes after midnight`) AT LEAST (served's `minutes after midnight`)
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (period in its own words): "after the expiration of 24 hours after the service of the notice"
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (period in its own words): "after the expiration of 24 hours after the service of the notice"

-- The same rule asked the other way round: from what moment may the bond be filed without consent?  Twenty-four hours after service is the same time of day on the next day.
@ref O 33 r 16(4) 24 hours (src:4767)
-- served: the moment the notice of bail was served.
GIVEN served IS A Moment
GIVETH A Moment
`o 33 r 16(4) the earliest moment the bond may be filed without consent` MEANS
    Moment WITH `day of the moment` IS (served's `day of the moment`) PLUS 1, `minutes after midnight` IS served's `minutes after midnight`

-- src:4769 | 17. —(1) Where property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court, a person who has an interest in that property or money but who is not a defendant to the action may, with the permission of the Court, intervene in the action. (2) An application for the grant of permission under this Rule must be made by summons without notice supported by an affidavit showing the interest of the applicant in the property against which the action is brought or in the money in Court.
@ref O 33 r 17(1) (src:4769)
GIVEN `property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an interest in that property or money and is not a defendant to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court gives permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 17(1) a person with an interest may intervene with the permission of the Court` MEANS
    IF `property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court` AND `the person has an interest in that property or money and is not a defendant to the action`
    THEN IF `the Court gives permission`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court, a person who has an interest in that property or money but who is not a defendant to the action may, with the permission of the Court, intervene in the action"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court, a person who has an interest in that property or money but who is not a defendant to the action may, with the permission of the Court, intervene in the action"
